ng the orderly wind-down of insolvent insurance companies in line with the Insurance Act.</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n<div class=\"pcf-page-content\">\r\n  <div class=\"pcf-page-main\">\r\n    <h2>When liquidation applies</h2>\r\n    <p>Where an insurer cannot be revived under statutory management and is ultimately declared insolvent, it may be placed under liquidation by court order. PCF\'s role at this stage is to compensate eligible policyholders and claimants for their unsettled claims.</p>\r\n    <h2>How to claim against an insurer in liquidation</h2>\r\n    <ol>\r\n      <li>Download the claims form from the PCF website, or collect one from PCF offices</li>\r\n      <li>Complete the form in duplicate and attach all required supporting documents</li>\r\n      <li>Submit to PCF for verification, approval, and processing</li>\r\n    </ol>\r\n    <p>Verification and approval typically takes approximately 30 days from submission.</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <aside class=\"pcf-page-sidebar\">\r\n    <div class=\"pcf-info-box\">\r\n      <h3>Quick facts</h3>\r\n      <dl>\r\n        <dt>Maximum payout</dt><dd>KSh 500,000 per claim (current statutory limit)</dd>\r\n        <dt>Verification time</dt><dd>Approximately 30 days</dd>\r\n        <dt>Legal basis</dt><dd>Section 179, Insurance Act (Cap 487)</dd>\r\n      </dl>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"pcf-cta-box\"><p>Ready to start your claim?</p><a href=\"/node/add/page\" class=\"pcf-btn pcf-btn--primary\">File a Claim</a></div>\r\n  </aside>\r\n</div>\";s:6:\"format\";s:9:\"full_html\";}}}s:17:\"field_description\";a:1:{s:9:\"x-default\";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{s:5:\"value\";s:11:\"Liquidation\";}}}}s:9:\"\0*\0fields\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0fieldDefinitions\";N;s:12:\"\0*\0languages\";N;s:14:\"\0*\0langcodeKey\";s:8:\"langcode\";s:21:\"\0*\0defaultLangcodeKey\";s:16:\"default_langcode\";s:17:\"\0*\0activeLangcode\";s:9:\"x-default\";s:28:\"\0*\0enforceDefaultTranslation\";N;s:18:\"\0*\0defaultLangcode\";s:2:\"en\";s:15:\"\0*\0tra